1. d4 e6 2. c4 c6 3. e4 h6 4. Nf3 d5 5. Bd3 dxe4 6. Bxe4 f5 7. Ne5 Bb4+ 8. Bd2 Bxd2+ 9. Nxd2 Nf6 10. Bf3 O-O 11. Nf1 Qc7 12. Qe2 Rd8 13. O-O-O Nbd7 14. Ng3 Nxe5 15. dxe5 Rxd1+ 16. Rxd1 Nd7 17. Rd6 Nf8 18. Nh5 Qa5 19. a3 Ng6 20. g4 Qxe5 21. Rd8+ Kf7 22. h3 Qc7 23. Qd2 f4 {Sources: The Field, 2 April 1887; The Chess Monthly, vol.8, 1886-87, p253. Position after Black's 23rd move, CM Grace v HS Robinson. The position proved the most difficult of all [for Zukertort to adjudicate]. Both players had conducted the game very slowly - four(!) hours for 23(!) moves.} (23... f4 {The most plausible continuation appeared to be} 24. Be4 Nf8 (24... e5 25. Bxg6+ Kxg6 26. Qd3+ Kf7 27. Rh8 {wins}) 25. Nxf4 (25. Qxf4+ Qxf4+ 26. Nxf4 Ke7) (25. Qd4 e5) 25... Ke7 $11) 1/2-1/2

